{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306893-an-orphan-archmage","id":1306893,"title":"An Orphan Archmage...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-22T10:31:00-07:00","id":1306893,"title":"An Orphan Archmage...","content":"Hi everybody, <br /> I have questioned this: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1280646-orphan-archmage\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...rphan-archmage</a><br /> <br /> Thanks to everybody's advice, I and my friends have made a character. Let me post it underneath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T10:31:37-07:00","id":1306894,"title":"","content":"Name: Moss &quot;Ratchet&quot; Charles <br /> Nature: Martyr <br /> Demeanor: Survivor <br /> Eseence: Primordial <br /> Tradition: Orphan <br /> <br /> Physical: Strength 2, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3 <br /> Social: Charisma 2, Manipulation 2, Appearance 3 Mental: Perception 4, Intelligence 4, Wits 3 <br /> <br /> Talents: Dodge 3, Awareness 3, Intimidation 2, Brawl 2, Athletics 1 <br /> Skills: Survival 3, Melee 2, Firearms 2, Stealth 2, Drive 2, Mediation 1, Do 1 <br /> Knowledges: Medicine 4, Occult 3, Computer 3, Lore (roughly All) 1, Linguistics 1, Science 1 <br /> <br /> Backgrounds: Avatar 3, Allies(Hunters) 3, Destiny 2, Arcane 2, Contacts 1<br /> <br /> Spheres: Prime 6, Life 4, Mind 3, Entropy 2, Spirit 1, Time 1 <br /> Willpower: 8 <br /> Arete: 6 <br /> Quintessence: 12 <br /> Paradox: 0<br /> <br /> Background: <br /> <br /> Moss was born the daughter of a perfect family in 1964, but everything changed when she was fifteen years old: A vampire broke into her house and killed her parents, Moss in tears hid in the wardrobe and had nothing to do--But she awakened. <br /> <br /> Moss, who was filled with remorse and angry, swore that she would revenge and killed this bloodsucker. She erased all her tracks and became an Orphan and a demon hunter. <br /> <br /> But learning more powerful magic isn't easy, she found, collected any resource as possible as she could. She used to meet many Supernaturals, and had a glimpse on the Word of Darkness. She also robbed some Tradition and Tech Union Chantries to fuel her own libraries. <br /> <br /> Now she thinks she already has a real understand of avoiding &quot;Bound&quot; (Aka. Paradox), and it's very useful to revenge. She recently joined a group of hunters as a doctor--After all, she is rather a human than a magician, and more guys in the same camp means more guarantee. <br /> <br /> Notes: <br /> <br /> 1. Seriously, Moss never knew anything like &quot;Umbra&quot; or &quot;Gauntlet&quot;, she spent all her life on Earth. But her Spirit 1 made her have a very infinite understand of spiritual things... <br /> <br /> 2. Moss doesn't receive very formal Magic training, so she may have some informal understanding of Magic. <br /> <br /> 3. Moss's Prime 6 explains why she can survive on Earth. And her Life 4 and Mind 3 could make her a good doctor. <br /> <br /> 4. Due to her Life 4 and Prime 6 and Mind 3, she has a 20's appearance. <br /> <br /> 5. She is alerted--won't use powerful magic in most public conditions. She knows that this World of Darkness is very dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 04-22-2019, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T10:42:48-07:00","id":1306897,"title":"","content":"Double post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 04-22-2019, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T12:17:34-07:00","id":1306936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306893-an-orphan-archmage?p=1306894#post1306894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Name: Moss &quot;Ratchet&quot; Charles<br /> 1. Seriously, Moss never knew anything like &quot;Umbra&quot; or &quot;Gauntlet&quot;, she spent all her life on Earth. But her Spirit 1 made her have a very infinite understand of spiritual things...</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirit 1 doesn't represent a very infinite understanding about anything. That would be represented trough Cosmology Knowledge and a greater understanding of the Sphere, among other things. Spirit 1 represents a dabbling on spiritual matters.<br /> <br /> It's very hard to believe that a mage that spent the time &amp; effort to study and get to Archmaster wouldn't at least <i>heard </i>about the Umbra. Heck, even some Hunters have <i>heard </i>about it (even if they can't get there, they know mages and ghosts flee to &quot;somewhere&quot;).<br /> <br /> It would be more believable if the mage knows plenty but doesn't <i>believe </i>in &quot;traveling&quot; to the other worlds (or at least not physically). Or she does believe and know, but doesn't want to go there because she thinks the good fight it's on earth and dedicating time to travel the spirit worlds it's a loss of time<br /> <br /> A word on Spirit for a Demon Hunter:<br /> <br /> Being limited to Spirit 1 would be very problematic when dealing with demonic Umbrood. You need at least 2 to affect them when they're on the other side, and up to 4 to exorcize someone and to bind demons so they can't cause mischief anymore. So you would be limited to hunt demons from Demon (and even then only when they're not on the Dark Umbra) and the possessed. Even in the case of eartly demons the power to bind a soul would be very useful to avoid their power to just go and possess other people to fight you again, and again, and again.<br /> <br /> I think it would be very frustrating to be a demon hunter w/o Spirit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Moss doesn't receive very formal Magic training, so she may have some informal understanding of Magic. </div> </div> </div><i>Some </i>informal understanding?, more like <i>a lot</i> of informal understanding....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-22-2019, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T14:05:15-07:00","id":1306972,"title":"","content":"I have some thoughts on this matter.<br /> <br /> 1) It is not bound need for a mage being in a tradition or other groups to able to become an archmage, but lets be real\u00edstic here, even when you get suport from a faction mages have really high mortality rate, imagine when you get.NO ONE to.even explain whats paradox or how.your magick is affected by It.<br /> <br /> 2) Even in traditions having Prime on high lvls are rare,.then an archmage of it is even more rare because of how abstract it tends to be. Not only did she attain high arete she did also something that even people with backup of an entire organization rarely afford.<br /> <br /> 3) Why would someone invest so heavily on Prime without having a really, REALLY good motivation for such? Its not the best suited for a vengeful hunter, even Matter would've made more Sense. And she survived with no dot on Forces considering that her nemesis is a vampire... Hard to beliave.<br /> <br /> The question is, why do you need an orphan archamage, or even why a prime archmage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24274,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","user":"menos125","date":". 04-22-2019, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","name":"menos125","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T14:07:33-07:00","id":1306975,"title":"","content":"Not a frequent guy around here, but if I would build a Orphan Archmage I would go for a less explosive magic than Prime, maybe Mind or Spirit (Aleph gave good reasons for Spirit). I would go for Entropy, an Chaos Magician working with the universe on her side... avoiding Paradox by the use of minimal vulgar magic...<br /> <br /> Not telling it\u2019s impossible, but Prime is probably the most complex sphere to master without \u201cformal training\u201d as it deals with Magick itself, not an aspect of the world...<br /> I know Prime sound good for hunting demons, but you still need to affect if it\u2019s not material, and need a way to shield you from their powers, I am not sure if Parma Magica would be useful against demons attacks...<br /> <br /> Item 5, man, that\u2019s beyond my view of possible... if she is archmage of Prime, she is capable of shielding against paradox, it\u2019s not a \u201cI avoid this because it\u2019s bad\u201d it\u2019s more like \u201cBound is a annoying thing I learned to control, why didn\u2019t you?\u201d. She may have an informal learning, but she knows ALL about paradox to get to Prime 6...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T22:00:23-07:00","id":1307142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306893-an-orphan-archmage?p=1306936#post1306936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit 1 doesn't represent a very infinite understanding about anything. That would be represented trough Cosmology Knowledge and a greater understanding of the Sphere, among other things. Spirit 1 represents a dabbling on spiritual matters.<br /> <br /> It's very hard to believe that a mage that spent the time &amp; effort to study and get to Archmaster wouldn't at least <i>heard </i>about the Umbra. Heck, even some Hunters have <i>heard </i>about it (even if they can't get there, they know mages and ghosts flee to &quot;somewhere&quot;).<br /> <br /> It would be more believable if the mage knows plenty but doesn't <i>believe </i>in &quot;traveling&quot; to the other worlds (or at least not physically). Or she does believe and know, but doesn't want to go there because she thinks the good fight it's on earth and dedicating time to travel the spirit worlds it's a loss of time. </div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks to your advice. We should specify more about her.<br /> <br /> First she DOES KNOW that there is a spiritual world which has many strange things, and some mages or &quot;beastmen&quot; flee to it from time to time. But she DOES NOT KNOW that this world is called &quot;Umbra&quot; or any other name which organized mages use. That's so called &quot;infinite&quot;. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306893-an-orphan-archmage?p=1306936#post1306936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A word on Spirit for a Demon Hunter:<br /> <br /> Being limited to Spirit 1 would be very problematic when dealing with demonic Umbrood. You need at least 2 to affect them when they're on the other side, and up to 4 to exorcize someone and to bind demons so they can't cause mischief anymore. So you would be limited to hunt demons from Demon (and even then only when they're not on the Dark Umbra) and the possessed. Even in the case of eartly demons the power to bind a soul would be very useful to avoid their power to just go and possess other people to fight you again, and again, and again.<br /> <br /> I think it would be very frustrating to be a demon hunter w/o Spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry that's our mistake. She is rather a &quot;Supernatural Hunter&quot; than a &quot;Demon Hunter&quot;. She hunts all kinds of supernaturals, especially those incline to harm mortals. <br /> <br /> I guess the &quot;Demon&quot; you talk about is Umbral beings resemble Demon, which is explained in The Infinity Tapestry (Mage's Demon isn't exactly Fallen Angels in D:tF!). But this may be unnecessary for her...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>menos125</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306893-an-orphan-archmage?p=1306972#post1306972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) It is not bound need for a mage being in a tradition or other groups to able to become an archmage, but lets be real\u00edstic here, even when you get suport from a faction mages have really high mortality rate, imagine when you get.NO ONE to.even explain whats paradox or how.your magick is affected by It.</div> </div> </div> </div>She is a robber to organized mages. What she will learn depends on what she have robbed... but you're right, we should let her have some formal understanding of basic things...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>menos125</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306893-an-orphan-archmage?p=1306972#post1306972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Even in traditions having Prime on high lvls are rare,.then an archmage of it is even more rare because of how abstract it tends to be. Not only did she attain high arete she did also something that even people with backup of an entire organization rarely afford.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think she specializes in Prime can be explained by &quot;Talents&quot; or something, depending on my friend.<br /> <br /> And, to be honest she will be a Pillar in hunter groups, you see she joined them as a doctor and her title &quot;Ratchet&quot;(coming from Transformers...), she will be a logistician.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>menos125</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306893-an-orphan-archmage?p=1306972#post1306972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question is, why do you need an orphan archamage, or even why a prime archmage?</div> </div> </div> </div>My friend's request. But maybe I will suggest him creating lesser and more suitable NPC... this guy... may become problematic during games...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306893-an-orphan-archmage?p=1306975#post1306975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a frequent guy around here, but if I would build a Orphan Archmage I would go for a less explosive magic than Prime, maybe Mind or Spirit (Aleph gave good reasons for Spirit). I would go for Entropy, an Chaos Magician working with the universe on her side... avoiding Paradox by the use of minimal vulgar magic...</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh to be honest you're much more frequent than me...<br /> <br /> And, the reasons why my friend choose Prime to be her Archsphere are(I didn't take a part in it):<br /> <br /> 1. Prime can deal more with hunters (anyway).<br /> <br /> 2. Prime can wash Paradox more efficiently. After all Archspheres are always vulgar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 04-23-2019, 01:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T04:10:44-07:00","id":1307193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>menos125</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306893-an-orphan-archmage?p=1306972#post1306972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Why would someone invest so heavily on Prime without having a really, REALLY good motivation for such?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't quite follow that reasoning.<br /> A simple cause for 'investing' into Prime that much (And remember, that's not quite how the in.game thoughts go..) might be a simple, personal absolute fascination with the fifth essence and the flow of magic between..well. Everything. The character does not need to consider the viability in the game. I consider any sphere as valid as the other, for having a character wanting to get lost in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T10:51:02-07:00","id":1307250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306893-an-orphan-archmage?p=1307142#post1307142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry that's our mistake. She is rather a &quot;Supernatural Hunter&quot; than a &quot;Demon Hunter&quot;. She hunts all kinds of supernaturals, especially those incline to harm mortals.<br /> <br /> I guess the &quot;Demon&quot; you talk about is Umbral beings resemble Demon, which is explained in The Infinity Tapestry (Mage's Demon isn't exactly Fallen Angels in D:tF!). But this may be unnecessary for her...</div> </div> </div> </div>When I talk about &quot;Umbral beings resemble Demon&quot; I say &quot;demonic Umbrood&quot;. When I say &quot;demons from Demon&quot; I mean a D:tF demon, these can go into the Umbra too (Slayers in particular), but are less attached to it. D:tF Fallen Angels are capable of possessing another host when their body it's killed, King Solomon among other occultists were able to deal with this by binding these demons in prissions they weren't able to escape. Where there aren't explicit Mage rules for this, I would guestimate that with less than Spirit 4 she ain't going to be able do it.<br /> <br /> Also I'm guessing she never hunted Specters either, since she can't affect these directly w/o Spirit 2+.<br /> <br /> It's worth to note that many Hunter Edges can traverse the Gauntlet and affect the beings on the other side. Maybe that's why the player feels this power to be unnecessary (it's not like <i>the party</i> won't be able to tackle ghosts otherwise).<br /> <br /> Still I mantain that if you hunt the supernatural in general, expending a few points in Spirit it's far from useless","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-23-2019, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T16:37:12-07:00","id":1307332,"title":"","content":"If demon hunter includes vampires, it's odd to me that one would lack Matter as a vampire hunter or more spirit for demons. But if they're an orphan. Eeeeh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T09:21:03-07:00","id":1307497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306893-an-orphan-archmage?p=1307250#post1307250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When I talk about &amp;quot;Umbral beings resemble Demon&amp;quot; I say &amp;quot;demonic Umbrood&amp;quot;. When I say &amp;quot;demons from Demon&amp;quot; I mean a D:tF demon, these can go into the Umbra too (Slayers in particular), but are less attached to it. D:tF Fallen Angels are capable of possessing another host when their body it's killed, King Solomon among other occultists were able to deal with this by binding these demons in prissions they weren't able to escape. Where there aren't explicit Mage rules for this, I would guestimate that with less than Spirit 4 she ain't going to be able do it.<br /> <br /> Also I'm guessing she never hunted Specters either, since she can't affect these directly w/o Spirit 2+.<br /> <br /> It's worth to note that many Hunter Edges can traverse the Gauntlet and affect the beings on the other side. Maybe that's why the player feels this power to be unnecessary (it's not like <i>the party</i> won't be able to tackle ghosts otherwise).<br /> <br /> Still I mantain that if you hunt the supernatural in general, expending a few points in Spirit it's far from useless</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. But after all she is an Orphan Archmage and joins the hunters as a doctor. So we think she should have more or less dots on Sheets compared to rules in Masters of the Art, including Spheres. And invest more on Mind and Life... If she has high level Sprit and a few dots on Force or Matter as others said...she will overshadow hunters obviously. But we will consider this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T09:53:56-07:00","id":1307506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306893-an-orphan-archmage?p=1307497#post1307497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're right. But after all she is an Orphan Archmage and joins the hunters as a doctor. So we think she should have more or less dots on Sheets compared to rules in Masters of the Art, including Spheres. And invest more on Mind and Life... If she has high level Sprit and a few dots on Force or Matter as others said...she will overshadow hunters obviously. But we will consider this.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I <i>really </i>don't like those char-gen rules :P<br /> <br /> I think the only way for her to not be OP as it is, it's if the player doesn't want to play strategically and RPs in a way that doesn't overhadow the others . She's an Archmaster for christ sake. Of course she's going to be OP. Spheres at 5 already break most games. <i>Spheres</i> break comon notions of &quot;game balance&quot; when used cleverly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-24-2019, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T10:06:19-07:00","id":1307510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306893-an-orphan-archmage?p=1307506#post1307506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I <i>really </i>don't like those char-gen rules :P</div> </div> </div> </div>We also dislike it, but to be honest an Orphan Archmage can't be very powerful, and Archmage creation in that book is... suitable, at least we think so...<br /> <br /> PS: What's your opinion about others?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T11:49:52-07:00","id":1307548,"title":"","content":"I have yet to see a system to create <i>Archmasters </i>that I like...I preffer the systems of Vampire to create Elders with a fixed amount of Freebies/XP<br /> <br /> I've always seen Ibn-Thot as a somewhat of a &quot;mild&quot; Archmage. He doesn't have ALL Spheres (which it's supposed to be rare among Archmages according to MotA fluff) but has most of them and impresive Attributes. No other canon Archmage that I know it's weaker in terms of Spheres, but probably there are weaker ones. I think that a trully &quot;weak&quot; Archmaster should be inferior to Ibn-Thot, but not by a long shot.<br /> <br /> But you're right in that such character feels WAY too OP for a Hunter chronicle, even with Extremists. The thing it's...to me wanting to play Archmaster and not wanting to be OP it's an oximoron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T18:36:31-07:00","id":1307646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306893-an-orphan-archmage?p=1307548#post1307548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have yet to see a system to create <i>Archmasters </i>that I like...I preffer the systems of Vampire to create Elders with a fixed amount of Freebies/XP</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh to be honest I do want to ask a question: Why do you usually compare Archmages to Vampire Elders?<br /> <br /> Sure they are true elders in mage community. But, they are also Ascension War and All Organization Leaders, much like Meths in Jyhad. On the other hand, Archspheres can be equal to Lv.7-9 Disciplines even in the VtM ST Handbook Re., which obviously steer much more to Vampires.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, Lv.5 Master is more equal to &quot;Elder&quot;, and Lv.6 Archmage should be equal to top elder and Meths, Oracle, of course, it's Antes...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306893-an-orphan-archmage?p=1307548#post1307548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you're right in that such character feels WAY too OP for a Hunter chronicle, even with Extremists. The thing it's...to me wanting to play Archmaster and not wanting to be OP it's an oximoron.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my opinion, hunters are weak, at least in Physics.<br /> <br /> Their Edges are also... reluctant compared to other Races' powers.<br /> <br /> They are limited in investing Edges, Vampires may have several Lv.5 Disciplines, which are cheap and appreciable. But as a hunter you may have Lv.3 Edge at most(They are also not cheap), and it is not difficult for many other races to counter these powers. Only some excellent hunters could have just one Lv.4 Edges(In my memory only God45 among Canon NPCs has a Lv.4 Edges--and he affords a lot for it, I haven't seen NPC with Lv.5 Edge).<br /> <br /> Although getting highest level Edges is accessible in System according to some extended books(One is to become an Extremist, another one I remember is to modify Edge systems to get purchasing Lv.5 Edges accessible, which is mentioned in ST Handbook or others.) But, it will have many other problems, lots of flaws will be added to your character, and to be honest their powers aren't really impressive... you afford much more than you actually get.<br /> <br /> And Edges &quot;Strength&quot; isn't decided by level, some Lv.4-5 Edges are strange, which means they may not be very efficient when facing enemies.<br /> <br /> Yes, Edges decide hunters should be in group to face enemies, but they should have really powerful Edges to take really powerful guys down. After all &quot;Level vs Level&quot; is also used in HtR(Mages' Prime 4 can counter Lv.3 Edges, which means a avearge Celestial Chorus Adept could defeat most hunters...)<br /> <br /> That's why we invest this Orphan's Sphere very carefully. Only ONE Lv.4 Sphere means A LOT to hunters...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 04-25-2019, 01:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T07:00:34-07:00","id":1307743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh to be honest I do want to ask a question: Why do you usually compare Archmages to Vampire Elders?<br /> <br /> Sure they are true elders in mage community. But, they are also Ascension War and All Organization Leaders, much like Meths in Jyhad. On the other hand, Archspheres can be equal to Lv.7-9 Disciplines even in the VtM ST Handbook Re., which obviously steer much more to Vampires.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, Lv.5 Master is more equal to &quot;Elder&quot;, and Lv.6 Archmage should be equal to top elder and Meths, Oracle, of course, it's Antes...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, well. I was generalizing about &quot;elders&quot; (Meths are called elders sometimes, with their Ante being &quot;the eldest&quot;). But I think you're right, there may be some gray areas but in general your reasoning it's sound. Nothing to add there.<br /> <br /> However, my point was to give them an amount of XP and a few guidelines. I wasn't trying to make a power scaling argument.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In my opinion, hunters are weak, at least in Physics. </div> </div> </div>Well, Hunter it's a very &quot;street level&quot; game. Mosters are suposed to be scary for the hunters, that's a general theme that runs trough most Hunter books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-25-2019, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T08:10:52-07:00","id":1307760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306893-an-orphan-archmage?p=1307743#post1307743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, well. I was generalizing about &quot;elders&quot; (Meths are called elders sometimes, with their Ante being &quot;the eldest&quot;). But I think you're right, there may be some gray areas but in general your reasoning it's sound. Nothing to add there.<br /> <br /> However, my point was to give them an amount of XP and a few guidelines. I wasn't trying to make a power scaling argument.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well, Hunter it's a very &quot;street level&quot; game. Mosters are suposed to be scary for the hunters, that's a general theme that runs trough most Hunter books.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you say is right, I should discuss this in a more private way, not here. Deflecting theme is improper.<br /> <br /> Thanks for your listening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 04-25-2019, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{